== ARCHIVE: suite state after the CCSD(T) refactor - 49 fast tests run, 20 slow carried ==

Collection, measured: 69 tests in the working tree = 49 under `-m "not slow"` + 20 under
`-m slow`.

What was actually executed here, and what was not (the numbers below are the archived
second execution; a first one gave 49 passed in 27.25 s and 4 passed in 0.54 s):

    $ PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m pytest -m "not slow" -q
    49 passed, 20 deselected in 26.13s

    $ PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m pytest nlcsplit/tests/test_cc_convention.py -q
    4 passed in 0.28s

The 20 slow tests were NOT re-run, and that is a claim with a checkable justification
rather than a convenience. `git diff --name-only afdefba HEAD -- nlcsplit/` returns exactly
one path, `nlcsplit/step_m_ccsdt.py`, and the working tree adds one more,
`nlcsplit/tests/test_cc_convention.py`. (afdefba is the commit whose tree the archived
65-test full run measured - `20260930T202235Z_suite65_full_and_counts.out`, 65 passed,
710.73 s, whose header prints the `git status` of that tree.) Nothing the slow tests import
moved: nlc.py, partition.py, fastpair.py, geomlib.py and step_f_dispersion.py are
byte-identical between the two states, so re-running them would re-measure code that
has not changed and would cost ~700 s of SCF plus O(N^2) double sums to do it. The slow
result therefore carries over from the archived full run, and that carry-over is stated
here rather than hidden behind a "69 passed" line that was never executed.

One methodological note, because the first attempt at the diff-surface check produced a
false answer: comparing `git show <commit>:file | sha256sum` against `sha256sum file` on
this working tree reports differences for files nobody touched, because Git normalises
LF/CRLF between the blob and the checkout. The blob-to-blob `git diff --name-only` above
is the version that means what it says.

Environment: PySCF 2.12.1, Python 3.10.12 (WSL), numpy 2.2.6, scipy 1.15.3.
Python module imports inside the tests are unchanged from that run.

